course: dictionary
lesson: 3498
title: Places and their words
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A farmyard is the area round the farm buildings, often with animals and machines in it. You can work out what it means from the words around it. Read this: «their great-great-grandchildren scratch for worms in the farmyard today». Birds scratch for worms in the ground, so a farmyard must be an outdoor place where animals find food.
explain: Look for clues in phrases too. «Farmyard animals» tells you the animals belong with a farm, such as hens, cows, pigs, sheep, ducks and horses. «Farmyard noises» tells you the sounds those animals make. The word farmyard is the same whether it describes a place or the animals, but the clues show which one it is.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Try «The hens scratched for worms in the farm buildings», and then «in the farmyard». Both fit, so the farm buildings and the area around them are close in meaning. If your meaning makes the sentence strange, go back and look at the clues again.
fact: A farmyard is the area round the farm buildings.
fact: Farmyards often have animals and machines in them.
fact: «Farmyard animals» means animals that live on a farm, such as hens, cows, pigs, sheep, ducks and horses.
fact: «Farmyard noises» means the sounds that farm animals make.
fact: A context clue is a word or phrase near an unknown word that helps you find its meaning.
exercise: Where do the great-great-grandchildren scratch for worms? «...scratch for worms in the farmyard today» | *In a farmyard | In a desert | In a museum | Under the sea
exercise: What is a farmyard? | A large field of wheat with no buildings at all | A shop that sells eggs and milk | A room inside a farmhouse | *An area round the farm buildings, often with animals and machines in it
exercise: In the phrase «farmyard animals», which animal could it be? | A shark | A penguin | A lion | *A hen
test: What are «farmyard noises»? | *The sounds that farm animals make | Noises made by cars on a busy road | The sounds of waves on a beach | Music played at a farm show
test: Which of these is a machine you might find in a farmyard? | A toaster | *A tractor | A kettle | A bicycle
exam: Which sentence uses farmyard correctly? | The farmyard swam in the sea. | The farmyard sang a song to the moon. | *The hens ran across the farmyard to get their food. | I ate a farmyard for breakfast.
